# Reference Gaps v38

Unapproved layout concept, built-in image generation using v36 Planar_Master as reference. Four unequal banks separated by black sky gaps. Second pass removes radial spikes and corrects upper-left crown direction. Generated proportions are visual approximations, not exact preservation of the source pixels or aspect ratio. v37 deterministic source projection remains intact. No level replacement, independent alpha not authored.

## Initial prompt

Create a square polar UV cloud atlas using the attached approved planar cloud painting as the shape and proportion reference. Preserve its natural WIDE LOW proportions and restrained flat painted gray planes. Add a few similar cloud banks, not repetitions. Do not stretch the original cloud strip around a whole circle.
Layout: four unequal separated elongated cloud groups near outer polar radius. One substantial reference-like bank in right quadrant, one lower thinner bank at bottom-left, a small shallow distant bank at upper-left, another medium wide bank near top. Leave LARGE black angular gaps between these groups, totaling roughly half of the circumference. Broad empty central sky. No closed ring, no connected donut, no cloud carpet.
Each bank must have the same width-to-height feeling as the planar reference: broad flat bases and long connected unequal rises, big quiet shadow surfaces, a few pale broad cap planes. Do not compress wide clouds into tall blobs. Keep source-like silhouettes with shallow unevenness and long calm curves. No tiny repeating scallops or cauliflower paint marks.
MANDATORY POLAR ORIENTATION: each bank is a BENT HORIZONTAL STRIP running TANGENTIALLY around circumference. Clouds' TOPS face center; BASES face outward. At right bank tops point LEFT and base RIGHT; top bank tops DOWN base UP; bottom bank tops UP base DOWN; left bank tops RIGHT base LEFT. All long tail shapes and shadow shelves follow arcs concentric with center, never point radially into center and never retain screen-horizontal orientation on side banks. Light faces center; broad darker underside near exterior.
Finish both ends of each bank naturally with short tangential taper or calm rounded forms; no sliced straight endpoint, no giant knife-like wisps. Do not add extra modules to fill empty areas. Pure opaque black background and clear black margin. Grayscale only, no alpha checkerboard, no labels, no scene objects. Broad tonal planes, subtle soft transitions, no outlines or bright rims. Preserve original cloud design language and proportions; infer additional groups conservatively.

## Correction

Make a targeted correction to this four-bank polar cloud atlas. Preserve four-bank layout, all large black gaps, each bank width and thickness, and flat tonal planes. Fix upper-left bank: its pale rounded crown currently faces upper-left exterior. It must face DOWN-RIGHT toward exact canvas center; dark flat underside faces UP-LEFT exterior. Reverse that bank's radial cross-section only.
Remove every sharp long spike pointing radially into central sky, especially the right bank's left-pointing horizontal tongues. Replace these spikes with quiet continuous rounded silhouette shoulders, not new puffs. Tail extensions may exist ONLY at the two angular ends of each bank and must be SHORT, TANGENTIAL and gently curved with circumference. Right-bank tails point roughly up/down along circular arc, NOT left into center. No long knife-like streaks anywhere. Preserve natural cloud proportions, do not turn banks into skinny crescents or thicken them. Preserve large empty center and black gaps. Keep broad flat shadow masses and restrained detail, no added serrations, strokes, text or outlines.
